    {
      "id": 8712245256622475,
      "plugin": "Cardinal",
      "model": "TextEditor",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "pos": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "params": [],
      "data": {
        "filepath": "",
        "lang": "None",
        "etext": "MINI ARRANGER  (mini bianquji)\n================================\n\nROW 1: CLOCK BUTTONS KEYS | PIANO ROLL | VCO ADSR VCA OUT\nROW 2: this note + MIDI CC map\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. Press RUN (small button left of the keys),\n   the roll starts rolling.\n2. Press REC once -> recording is armed\n   (press again to stop recording).\n3. Play the SMK-25 keys. Notes land on the grid\n   AND you hear them while you play.\n4. Press RUN again to stop. Notes stay in the patch.\n5. Right-click the roll: Clear / Copy / Paste,\n   Notes to Show, Driver Mode, Clock Delay.\n\nSIGNAL PATH\nkeys -> PianoRoll -> VCO -> VCA -> HostAudio2\nClocked OUT1 (16th notes) -> PianoRoll CLOCK\nbuttons -> PianoRoll RUN / RECORD\n\nKNOBS\nClocked  Master clock  = tempo (BPM)\nClocked  Clk 1 ratio   = 5  -> x4 (16th notes)\nVCO      Frequency / Pulse width\nADSR     A D S R\nVCA-1    Channel 1 level\nHostAudio2  Level\n\nNOTES\n* The roll records ONE note at a time (mono).\n* Gate stays high across steps, so RETRIGGER\n  drives the envelope (that is why OUT7 is wired\n  to ADSR RETRIG).\n* END_OF_PATTERN output = chain a 2nd roll:\n  OUT9 -> next roll RUN, OUT0 -> next roll CLOCK.\n",
        "width": 26
      }
    },
